  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_049: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted; acc=0.725) shows consistent gains from each design upgrade (scvi>pca, ViT>ResNet, weighted>concat, transformer>avgpool). However, the fusion effect was only validated with avgpool aggregation (config_005 vs config_007: +0.046). With transformer aggregation, the learned attention mechanism may already capture modality-level weighting, potentially making explicit weighted fusion redundant. Question: Does weighted fusion still provide a meaningful advantage over simple concat when paired with transformer aggregation? config_009 is identical to config_049 except fusion=concat, giving a clean single-variable A/B test. Why best next: It directly clarifies whether one of our key design choices (weighted fusion) is truly necessary or subsumed by the transformer, which affects both final architecture complexity and whether further fusion-level exploration is warranted. Under a limited budget, isolating this interaction at the top-performing configuration is more informative than jumping to an untested RNA encoder (scgpt) that would confound multiple variables."
}

